15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram illustrating a neural network architecture for object detection in wheat images, with labeled modules such as conv, down, upsample, FCM, C2PSA, and detection heads. The input section shows a wheat field image, while the output section displays the same image with multiple blue bounding boxes and confidence scores marking detected wheat heads.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Diagram of five neural network module architectures labeled A to E, each within dashed borders and color-coded backgrounds. Panel A \(yellow\) presents FCM with input split, series of convolutions, cross attention combining channel and spatial attention, and output. Panel B \(purple\) shows MKP with stacked depthwise and pointwise convolutions of increasing kernel size. Panel C \(peach\) illustrates C3k2 with convolution, split, multiple bottleneck layers, concatenation, and final convolution, with a variant path indicated. Panel D \(blue\) displays SPPF with convolution, three sequential max pooling layers merged then convolved, with optional addition. Panel E \(light blue\) depicts C2PSA with convolution, split, repeated PSA blocks, concatenation, and final convolution.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Ten columns of plant images arranged in five rows, each column labeled from Image number zero to Image number nine. The first row displays original images of grass-like plants. The second and third rows show the same images with overlaid blue detection boxes and labels from YOLO26 Det and LiteMS Det methods respectively. The fourth and fifth rows present multi-colored heatmaps with red-outlined detection boxes representing YOLO26 and LiteMS-YOLO model heatmaps. Each model visualizes detection or heatmap differences across various plant images.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side comparison of wheat detection using two object detection models, YOLO26n on the left and LiteMS-YOLO on the right, with blue bounding boxes and confidence scores overlaid on wheat heads within green foliage. Red circles highlight missed detections or inaccuracies in the left image, while the right image shows more detected objects with varying confidence values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Ten-panel grid of training progress graphs showing loss and performance metrics over epochs for a machine learning model. Top row: training box loss, classification loss, DFL loss, precision, and recall improve steadily. Bottom row: validation box loss, classification loss, DFL loss, mAP50, and mAP50-95 also show clear improvement, with metrics rising and losses decreasing. Dotted lines represent smoothed trends.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side confusion matrix and normalized confusion matrix heatmaps for two classes: Wheat Spike and Background. The left matrix shows count values; the right, normalized values with highest accuracy for true Background prediction.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Two-panel graphic showing evaluation curves for a classification model. Left panel is a precision-recall curve with precision remaining high until recall approaches one, mean average precision of zero point nine two eight. Right panel is an F1-confidence curve peaking at zero point eight nine F1 score at confidence zero point two eight four, with a sharp decline at higher confidence thresholds. Both graphs display results for all classes in blue and a legend in the lower left corner.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Quadcopter drone with four propellers flying against a clear blue sky, featuring camera equipment and landing gear visible in silhouette.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Diagram with two labeled panels showing a drone flying above crops at a height of three meters and a distance of six meters from the ground area marked as low-altitude turbulence. Panel A shows the drone without wind, while panel B shows wind indicated by arrows blowing toward the drone. Both panels display a forty-five degree angle from the drone to the edge of the affected area.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
